{
  "id": 177299909,
  "iid": 8153,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "GIOP and idl2wrs: Implementation of Any type and fixes and improvements for idl2wrs",
  "description": "It is now possible to recursively process the any-type in GIOP.\nAdded an additional restriction on picking subdissectors for\nGIOP. Since there can be multiple operations with the same name\ninside the various IDLs, it is necessary to properly determine\nwhich interface was actually meant in the packet. Thus it will only\npick the subdissector which returns True on the operation name\nand processes all the bytes of the packet as a simple heuristic\nmetric. Given this method, there is still a possibility of falsely\npicked subdissectors in complex interfaces in Corba, if they also\nmanage to fit all the remaining bytes into their parameters.\n\nidl2wrs has generated subdissectors incorrectly, if entities\n(such as operations, structs ...) of the same\nname occur in an include. By reversing the lists for enums, structs,\noperations and exceptions it properly uses the right entities in the\ncurrent IDL, which are effectively the last occurrence of the\nentities. Previously idl2wrs would use the first occurrence of an\nentity, which has the same name. Those usually originate from an\ninclude pre-processor command instead of the intended IDL.\nSubtrees for structs, unions, arrays and sequences also have\nbeen implemented in this branch.",
  "state": "merged",
