    {
      "id": "8754325974719a57718db10067b7ceecca63d9cf",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1963963804,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There are several dissectors that were generated by the GIOP version of idl2wrs - `coseventcomm`, `cosnaming`, `gias`, and `tango`. They still need to be regenerated with the changed idl2wrs (though we also would presumably like to do the glib type changes as well.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-24T03:14:31.791Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-24T09:34:13.310Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 177299909,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 8153,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1964364501,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Are these interfaces part of wireshark (without adding custom plugins and we just have to update some c-files generated using idl2wrs? What do you mean with glib changes? What is glib?\n\nStarting mid july we have a new internship and could make contributions regarding this topic and improve idl2wrs further.",
          "author": {
            "id": 3906765,
            "username": "poldy79",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Leonard Penzer",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8baab4da8de764d192c97549dab04f21595708ebe50ed7af667c24cc16d4c423?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/poldy79"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-24T09:34:13.203Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-24T09:34:13.203Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 177299909,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 8153,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1964555697,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Yes, just use idl2wrs to update dissectors. The idl files are in `epan/dissectors/corba-idl`.\n\nThe glib changes are in #19116. The project was started before C99 fixed width types were widely available, and we want to move to using those - `uint32_t` instead if `guint32`, etc.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-24T11:23:46.548Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-24T11:23:46.548Z",
          "system": false,
