        "a39968cbc3bd7727bf6730254401cc6dc9fb1b2a"
      ],
      "title": "idl2wrs: implemented the generation of value_strings for unions",
      "message": "idl2wrs: implemented the generation of value_strings for unions\n\nNow Unions also get their on mnemonic values represented in the tree by\ngenerating and using a value_string for them, even if they don't use\nEnum for their discriminant.\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-20T10:56:53.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/09061b92400cc00a6fde82cba7260953e3cc46d4"
    },
    {
      "id": "a39968cbc3bd7727bf6730254401cc6dc9fb1b2a",
      "short_id": "a39968cb",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "6e0ca18a91be9ab02b3e754d0820c3ae77110cae"
      ],
      "title": "idl2wrs: implemented subtrees for arrays and sequences",
      "message": "idl2wrs: implemented subtrees for arrays and sequences\n\nThe generated subdissectors can now display arrays and sequences as\nsubtrees, including nested arrays and sequences.\nThe subtrees will be named after the type and the name of the field.\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-13T11:01:01.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/a39968cbc3bd7727bf6730254401cc6dc9fb1b2a"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e0ca18a91be9ab02b3e754d0820c3ae77110cae",
      "short_id": "6e0ca18a",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "c6d12f5a3ec27d3c3a6115e3b78ce33fa19793bf"
      ],
      "title": "GIOP: improved processing of enum type inside of \"Any\" type",
      "message": "GIOP: improved processing of enum type inside of \"Any\" type\n\nThe parameters of the enum typecode in Any are now properly used for\ndisplaying the mnemonic value of the said enum.\nAlso did some cleanup of my code for processing Any.\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-13T09:21:39.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/6e0ca18a91be9ab02b3e754d0820c3ae77110cae"
    },
    {
      "id": "c6d12f5a3ec27d3c3a6115e3b78ce33fa19793bf",
      "short_id": "c6d12f5a",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "fd36449cd465065204b29d2d2bf98dfe98f783bd"
      ],
      "title": "idl2wrs: Fix for enum dissector code generation in the idl2wrs backend",
      "message": "idl2wrs: Fix for enum dissector code generation in the idl2wrs backend\n\nwireshark_gen.py assumed that most of its get_CDR_xxx templates would\nleave a variable behind which could be used to save the discriminant\nto get the right data type from the union. Unfortunately this only held\ntrue for enum data type, not for long, short and so on.\nI fixed it by rewinding the offset for each data type and getting the\ndiscriminant via a get_CDR_xxx function\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-09T12:15:19.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/c6d12f5a3ec27d3c3a6115e3b78ce33fa19793bf"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd36449cd465065204b29d2d2bf98dfe98f783bd",
      "short_id": "fd36449c",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "6fd605a7ebf873d9687f773213d47d191005f801"
      ],
      "title": "idl2wrs: Changed the way how the giop subdissectors register their protocols",
      "message": "idl2wrs: Changed the way how the giop subdissectors register their protocols\n\nTo avoid naming conflicts on already registered protocols the prefix \"GIOP/\"\nhas been added to proto_register_protocol template, so that certain IDL names\ndo not conflict with existing protocol names\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-09T12:14:07.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/fd36449cd465065204b29d2d2bf98dfe98f783bd"
    },
    {
      "id": "6fd605a7ebf873d9687f773213d47d191005f801",
      "short_id": "6fd605a7",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "575903c5f06a7e8cb1bc3f6ca04c730d5143d2f2"
      ],
      "title": "idl2wrs: corrected to conversion of IDL to C dissector",
      "message": "idl2wrs: corrected to conversion of IDL to C dissector\n\nThere was a scoping problem within the backend wireshark_gen.py\nwhen it came to an include preprocessor command inside of an IDL. It\ntook the very first declaration of functions, structs and so on from\nan include if it matched the name of such an element in the currently\nprocessed IDL, ignoring the scope of these elements. This led to\neither incomplete or completely mismatched functions inside of the\nC dissectors. The fix was to reverse the lists of operations,\nstructs, etc.\nAlso added subtrees for unions and structs\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-09T12:17:19.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/6fd605a7ebf873d9687f773213d47d191005f801"
    },
    {
      "id": "575903c5f06a7e8cb1bc3f6ca04c730d5143d2f2",
      "short_id": "575903c5",
      "created_at": "2022-09-29T11:40:29.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "d8983b54ba52f46408c015e25856227831fdd534"
      ],
      "title": "GIOP: almost completed the processing of all types under the any-type",
      "message": "GIOP: almost completed the processing of all types under the any-type\n\nIt is now possible to recursively process the any-type in GIOP.\nAdded an additional restriction on picking subdissectors for\nGIOP. Since there can be multiple operations with the same name\ninside the various IDLs, it is necessary to properly determine,\nwhich interface was actually meant in the packet. Thus it will only\npick the subdissector, which returns True on the operation name\nand processes all the bytes of the packet, as a simple heuristic\nmetric. Given this method, there is still a possibility of falsely\npicked subdissectors on complex interfaces in Corba, if they also\nmanage to fit all the remaining bytes into their parameters\n",
      "author_name": "Jonas Blust",
      "author_email": "jonas.blust@rohde-schwarz.com",
      "authored_date": "2022-09-09T12:16:13.000+02:00",
